// THE SHARED BUTTON, flat. It was a copy of MUI's stock outlined button —
// uppercase, a 0.0892857143em tracking nobody chose, a near-black 87% border,
// and a box-shadow in the transition list — which is the look the rest of the
// site has been moving off. The paint now comes from the prose-form tokens
// (app/styles/prose-form.styl, injected into every stylesheet), so a button
// sits in the same ink and the same rules as every control around it.
//
// FLAT MEANS NO SHADOW AND NO RAISE, in the resting, hover and active states
// alike. A pressed button answers with a fill, not with a drop shadow and not
// with a transform — the two things that put a control back on a fake z-axis.
//
// Every hook the Button component can actually produce is preserved: __small,
// __text, __active and the .count badge.
//
// FOUR VARIANTS WERE DROPPED, and one of them is why the others were suspect.
// `__failure` painted its ground with `$failureColor`, which is defined in no
// stylesheet in this repo — stylus emits an undefined variable as a bare ident,
// so `background-color: failureColor` was invalid CSS the browser discarded and
// the variant had never once rendered a red button. Nothing in `app/` sets that
// class, or `__success`, or `__outline`. `__icon` is set only by
// `icon-button.js`, which does not also set `.button`, so the descendant rule
// here could never match it either. All four were removed rather than repaired:
// a token invented for a variant with no call site is a guess about a design
// decision nobody has made.
//
// The :not() chain keeps this off MUI's own buttons, which carry .button at
// several call sites and bring their own paint.
.button:not(.MuiButton-root):not(.MuiIconButton-root):not(.MuiFab-root):not(.MuiButtonBase-root)
  position relative
  display inline-flex
  align-items center
  justify-content center
  // $control_height, and box-sizing with it, so this lines up EXACTLY with a
  // text input beside it. The border is inside the box, which is what lets the
  // border go from transparent to visible on hover without the button growing.
  box-sizing border-box
  height $control_height
  min-width 30px
  padding 0 16px
  vertical-align middle
  text-align center
  font-family $prose_sans
  font-size 0.875rem
  font-weight 500
  // No tracking and no uppercase. Both were MUI's, and both are what made a
  // button read as a different typeface from the label beside it.
  letter-spacing 0
  color $prose_ink
  // A LIGHT FILL RATHER THAN AN OUTLINE. The button used to be defined by its
  // edge — a 1px near-black rule around nothing — which is the outlined-button
  // idiom and the heaviest way to draw a control that is rarely the point of
  // its surface. The fill carries the shape now and the border is invisible at
  // rest, so a row of buttons reads as a row of soft blocks rather than as a
  // row of boxes.
  background $control_fill
  background-image none
  // Transparent rather than absent: it holds the 1px in the box model, so the
  // hover state can colour it in without the button changing size.
  border 1px solid transparent
  border-radius $button_border_radius
  outline none
  cursor pointer
  transition background 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease, box-shadow 120ms ease

  // The press is a deeper fill, not a lift.
  &:active:not(:disabled)
  &:active:not([disabled])
    background rgba(23, 24, 26, 0.12)
    box-shadow none

  // THE HOVER IS THE MENU SECTIONS' LIFT, shared from variables.styl rather
  // than reproduced here. Gated on a fine pointer for the reason every hover
  // state should be: a touch device has no un-hover, so the lift would stick to
  // the last button tapped until something else was.
  @media (pointer: fine)
    &:hover:not(:disabled)
    &:hover:not([disabled])
      hover_lift()
      border-color $prose_rule_strong

  // The ring is the focus indicator rather than a colour swap alone: a border
  // that only changes hue is invisible to anyone who cannot separate the two.
  &:focus-visible
    border-color $prose_ink
    box-shadow 0 0 0 3px rgba(23, 24, 26, 0.08)

  &:disabled
  &[disabled]
    opacity 0.45
    cursor default
    user-select none

  + .button
    margin-left 8px

  .count
    position absolute
    top 3px
    right 5px
    margin 0
    padding 3px
    font-family $prose_mono
    font-size 8px
    line-height 5px
    border 0
    border-radius 99em
    background rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)

  // The quiet one in a pair, and the only variant with no fill and no lift. A
  // text button that carried the light ground would be a filled button with a
  // different name, and one that lifted on hover would be a filled button that
  // waited. It sits inside table rows, where a hard offset shadow under a
  // one-word action reads as the row itself moving. The ink is the whole
  // response, so both the base fill and the base lift are undone here.
  &.button__text
    color $prose_muted
    background transparent
    border-color transparent
    @media (pointer: fine)
      &:hover:not(:disabled)
      &:hover:not([disabled])
        color $prose_ink
        background transparent
        border-color transparent
        box-shadow none

  &.active
  &.button__active
    color $accentColor
    border-color $accentColor

  &.button__small
    height 26px
    padding 0 10px
    font-size 12px
